  "label": "Significance Testing For Cell Partitions",
  "related": [
    "sequencing-genome-dba8",
    "untitled-topic-1773",
    "spatial-hi-18ec"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [
    "transcriptomics"
  ],
  "slug": "learning-causation-2f3a",
  "summary": "SigDoTS and ProClust add formal significance testing to spatial domains and scRNA-seq clusters, merging overclustered groups instead of trusting heuristics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is replacing heuristic partitioning with statistically tested outputs. SigDoTS adds hypothesis testing with FWER control to spatial transcriptomics domain detection, retaining or merging candidate domains based on null simulations. ProClust tests scRNA-seq cluster significance, merging overclustered groups via log-concave cluster modelling and projection-based tests. CellSavior uses confidence-weighted merging within ensemble clustering for targeted scDNA-seq cell calling, matching CellFinder in 31 of 33 datasets. Adjacent work builds explicit probabilistic models. stochprofIC applies distributional regression to correct noise and batch effects when inferring state variability from mini-bulk and split-pool data. Echidna jointly infers copy number alterations from scRNA-seq and bulk WGS in a Bayesian hierarchy. Benchmarks and standardization mark where current practice falls short. Typical RNA-seq depths miss alternative splicing, precision-matrix estimators for differential co-expression are compared, and SigBridgeR unifies eight phenotype-associated subpopulation algorithms. Perturbation-screen papers (cardioid CRISPR time course, Perturb-Tags, Superb-seq) sit largely outside this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
